WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.420
Flight envelope protection cut fatal loss of control accidents, 91%, yet left pilot slower

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.940
to recover when automation handed the airplane back.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:14.640
This is unintended consequences, episode 159, an air bus over the Atlantic, the protections

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:19.920
built to stop the old accidents, the way airlines then flew those jets, the skills that

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.640
thinned out, the drills added later, and the share of the job a person must still be ready

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:32.920
to take. In June 2009, Air France flight 447, an Airbus A330, lost reliable air-speed

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:39.240
data. Eist Pito probes were the cause. The autopilot disconnected. The aircraft was already

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:44.847
in a high-altitude cruise. It entered a stall the crew did not arrest. France's Bureau

00:00:44.847 --> 00:00:50.927
donkets at Danalees, the BEA later documented sustained nose-up inputs after that disconnect.

00:00:51.587 --> 00:00:54.187
Those inputs drove the aircraft into a deep stall.

00:00:54.827 --> 00:01:00.227
The BEA report noted the absence of recent high-altitude manual handling practice as a contributing

00:01:00.227 --> 00:01:00.747
factor.

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:07.227
Over decades, systems that kept airplanes inside safe envelopes during 99.9% of routine

00:01:07.227 --> 00:01:13.367
flight also removed repeated chances to rehearse recognition, mode awareness, and control inputs.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:18.847
That rehearsal belonged to the remaining fraction of a percent when those envelopes no longer

00:01:18.847 --> 00:01:19.267
applied.

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:22.407
The result was not a sudden failure of technology.

00:01:22.967 --> 00:01:27.227
It was a gradual shift in what the human and the loop was still able to do without notice.

00:01:27.947 --> 00:01:33.187
Engineers at Airbus and Boeing, with regulators at the Federal Aviation Administration and

00:01:33.187 --> 00:01:38.087
the European Union Aviation Safety Agency, had been building toward that envelope for

00:01:38.087 --> 00:01:38.507
a reason.

00:01:39.127 --> 00:01:44.627
In the 1980s and 1990s, they introduced full authority digital engine controls, flight

00:01:44.627 --> 00:01:48.007
management systems, and envelope limiting fly-by-wire laws.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:53.567
The explicit goal was to eliminate the most common fatal pilot errors, controlled flight

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:57.607
into terrain, loss of control and flight, unstable approaches.

00:01:58.287 --> 00:02:01.007
The aircraft itself would refuse unsafe trajectories.

00:02:01.527 --> 00:02:03.287
The record they were looking at was stark.

00:02:03.867 --> 00:02:09.787
Between 1959 and the mid-1980s, human factors still dominated accident statistics.

00:02:10.287 --> 00:02:14.167
That remained true after ground proximity warning systems and better training.

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:18.807
Rational actors concluded that further automation would close the remaining gap.

00:02:19.347 --> 00:02:22.167
They measured the problem in concrete accident categories.

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:28.167
Adding layers of protection and auto-flight could prevent trajectories the pilot alone had not always avoided.

00:02:28.707 --> 00:02:31.467
No one at the time argued that pilots should stop flying.

00:02:32.007 --> 00:02:36.207
The premise was that the machine would handle the envelope while the crew retained oversight.

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:38.647
That division looked technically feasible.

00:02:39.147 --> 00:02:42.507
It also looks statistically justified by the data then available.

00:02:42.507 --> 00:02:48.347
Airbus launched the A320 family in 1988 with flight envelope protections that prevented

00:02:48.347 --> 00:02:53.607
stalls and excessive bank angles in normal law, Boeing followed with its own auto flight

00:02:53.607 --> 00:03:00.627
suites on the 777 and later types. Early data showed the expected gains. Airbus statistical

00:03:00.627 --> 00:03:06.787
summaries record an 87% drop in controlled flight into terrain fatal accidents. Once generation

00:03:06.787 --> 00:03:11.947
Operation III aircraft added glass cockpits, terrain awareness, and flight management computers.

00:03:12.707 --> 00:03:17.887
Airlines adopted policies that encouraged maximum use of the autopilot to reduce workload

00:03:17.887 --> 00:03:19.307
and standardize performance.

00:03:20.127 --> 00:03:25.987
Captain Warren Vanderberg of American Airlines began warning in 1997 that crews were becoming

00:03:25.987 --> 00:03:27.607
children of the magenta line.

00:03:28.147 --> 00:03:31.907
The industry's priority remained the measurable reduction in accident rates.

00:03:31.907 --> 00:03:35.847
training programs therefore emphasize mastery of the flight management

00:03:35.847 --> 00:03:39.367
computer and mode awareness rather than routine hand-flying.

00:03:39.947 --> 00:03:43.427
The data showed that the automated path produced fewer deviations.

00:03:43.947 --> 00:03:50.067
The logic was internally consistent. If the protections worked, the safest procedure was to stay inside them.

00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:56.367
Those same systems also removed routine opportunities for pilots to practice manual flight path management.

00:03:56.907 --> 00:04:00.827
A 2014 study from the National Aeronautics and Space Administration

00:04:00.827 --> 00:04:07.647
led by Stephen Casner, placed 16 airline pilots in a Boeing 747-400 simulator.

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:12.187
Cognitive skills decayed measurably after periods of heavy automation use.

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:16.407
Tracking position without a map display, integrating raw data,

00:04:17.007 --> 00:04:21.507
recognizing mode changes, basic instrument scanning remained relatively intact.

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:26.247
A later federal aviation administration cognitive skill degradation study,

00:04:26.247 --> 00:04:30.847
running from 2022 through 2024, found a related split.

00:04:31.347 --> 00:04:33.147
Declarative knowledge of flight management

00:04:33.147 --> 00:04:36.767
and auto-flight interactions faded faster than procedural memory

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:40.347
when pilots spent 12 to 24 months away from the line.

00:04:41.067 --> 00:04:44.807
Envelope protections handled nearly every departure, cruise, and arrival.

00:04:45.347 --> 00:04:48.567
The average line pilot therefore accumulated far fewer hours

00:04:48.567 --> 00:04:51.447
actually moving the controls through the full range of normal

00:04:51.447 --> 00:04:52.807
and abnormal attitudes.

00:04:52.807 --> 00:04:58.167
When the rare event occurred and the protections stepped aside, the crew faced a task whose

00:04:58.167 --> 00:05:01.787
cognitive and motor demands had not been rehearsed at the same frequency.

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:05.087
Second order effects showed up in training departments.

00:05:05.527 --> 00:05:10.087
Recurrent simulator sessions focused on automation management rather than raw hand-flying.

00:05:10.647 --> 00:05:14.067
That focus reinforced the dependency the sessions were meant to mitigate.

00:05:14.627 --> 00:05:16.087
The arithmetic was straightforward.

00:05:16.747 --> 00:05:21.067
Each additional percentage point of flight time spent inside protected modes reduced the

00:05:21.067 --> 00:05:23.947
sample of manual recoveries available for skill maintenance.

00:05:24.547 --> 00:05:27.687
The probability of an automation handback event stayed low.

00:05:28.207 --> 00:05:29.267
It never reached zero.

00:05:30.358 --> 00:05:36.178
Airbus issued a 2020 manual flying policy urging pilots to hand fly segments under safe conditions.

00:05:36.858 --> 00:05:42.418
The Federal Aviation Administration updated advisory circular 120-111.

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:48.418
The circular requires upset prevention and recovery training, including academic and simulator

00:05:48.418 --> 00:05:53.978
work on startle effects and energy management. Airlines began inserting deliberate hand-flying

00:05:53.978 --> 00:05:59.398
exercises. They also added line-oriented flight training scenarios that force crews to step

00:05:59.398 --> 00:06:05.498
down automation levels. These measures have not reversed the overall safety gain. Airbus 2025

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:11.318
accident statistics still show generation 4 aircraft maintaining the lowest loss of control rates.

00:06:11.858 --> 00:06:17.538
The correction itself requires ongoing reinforcement. The underlying automation continues to expand.

00:06:17.538 --> 00:06:20.978
The daily line environment still favors the protected path.

00:06:21.658 --> 00:06:26.118
Training departments now treat manual currency as something that must be scheduled and protected.

00:06:26.598 --> 00:06:30.098
They no longer assume it will occur naturally through normal operations.

00:06:31.223 --> 00:06:36.423
When Airbus and Boeing chose envelope protection, they rewarded the metric of prevented accidents.

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:42.383
The supervisory skill of rapid manual intervention went unmeasured, and therefore underpracticed.

00:06:42.383 --> 00:06:47.683
Vanderberg's 1997 training directive still stands as the operational countermeasure.

00:06:48.183 --> 00:06:51.943
Crews must be willing to disconnect at low altitude rather than troubleshoot.

00:06:52.503 --> 00:06:55.423
That directive restores the missing practice loop directly.

00:06:56.043 --> 00:07:00.603
Regulators and carriers now schedule recurrent manual flight segments and upset recovery

00:07:00.603 --> 00:07:02.123
drills for a specific reason.

00:07:02.703 --> 00:07:06.903
The original automation decision had removed those repetitions from daily operations.

00:07:07.503 --> 00:07:11.203
The same pattern appears whenever a new supervisory system is introduced.

00:07:11.203 --> 00:07:14.923
The quantity that improves is the one the machine now owns.

00:07:15.403 --> 00:07:19.643
The quantity that erodes is the one the human must still be able to seize without notice.

00:07:20.223 --> 00:07:25.423
What fraction of any new supervisory task will still require the human to intervene at full proficiency?

00:07:25.963 --> 00:07:30.203
And how will that proficiency be maintained once the system is trusted to handle the routine?

00:07:30.843 --> 00:07:32.563
And that's where today's story leaves us.

00:07:32.983 --> 00:07:36.323
If it changed how you see one everyday decision, that's the whole point.

